# Scene persistence

Editor uses Dexie (IndexedDB) for:
1. Linear history of `SceneSnapshot`s for undo/redo (capped at 80).
2. Binary blobs (image data URLs, segmentation masks) keyed by node id.

DB: `effects-scene-db`. Two tables (single migration, version 1):

```ts
snapshots: '++id, timestamp'
blobs:     'key, updatedAt'
```

## Snapshot shape (`apps/editor/src/scene-store.ts`)

> Editor-only (Dexie). Supplier-app is in-memory + Export/Import. Re-exports `SerializedNode` / `SerializedEdge` from `@effects/runtime` so the wire format is shared with `PublishedPipeline.graph`.

```ts
SceneSnapshot {
  id?: number                // primary key
  timestamp: number          // Date.now()
  label: string              // 'edit' | 'import' | ...
  nodeIdCounter: number      // see "ID counter healing"
  manifestVersion?: number   // PUBLISH_MANIFEST_VERSION at write time;
                             //   defaults to 1 on read for legacy snapshots
  pinnedIds?: string[]
  pages?: SerializedPage[]
  activePageId?: string

  // DEPRECATED legacy flat fields. Read only by applySnapshot's
  // migration path when `pages` is missing — wraps into a single 'Main' page.
  // New writes always populate `pages`.
  nodes?: SerializedNode[]
  edges?: SerializedEdge[]
  viewport?: { x, y, zoom }
}

SerializedPage {
  id: string                 // 'p_<int>'
  name: string
  nodes: SerializedNode[]
  edges: SerializedEdge[]
  viewport?: { x, y, zoom }  // each page remembers its own zoom/pan
}

SerializedNode {
  id: string                 // 'n_<int>'
  type: string               // PROCESSOR_CATALOG key OR 'clone' for UI-only aliases
  position: { x, y }
  data: {
    processor: string        // 'clone' for clones, otherwise a real processor key
    params: Record<string, unknown>
    label?: string           // user-given display name
    cloneOf?: string         // UI-only viewer alias of another node anywhere in the scene;
                             //   engine NEVER sees clones — sceneResolver rewrites
                             //   clone-source edges to point at the original
    exposed?: {              // Tier-2 supplier metadata — see publish-plane.mdc
      mode: 'whole' | 'fields'
      fields?: string[]      // FieldDef.name keys when mode='fields' (config nodes)
      label?: string
      hint?: string
    }
    imageUrl?: string        // 'img:<nodeId>' blob key
    segPoints?: SamPoint[]
    segPolygon?: number[]    // SAM polygon, flat xy
    segMaskKey?: string      // 'seg:<nodeId>' blob key
    [key: string]: unknown
  }
  width?: number             // React Flow v12: NodeResizer writes top-level
  height?: number
  style?: Record<string, unknown>
  selected?: boolean
}

SerializedEdge {
  id?: string
  type?: string              // 'editableStep' for the live edge
  source: string
  sourceHandle?: string | null
  target: string
  targetHandle?: string | null
  data?: Record<string, unknown>   // EditableStepEdge: { bends: { x, y }[] }
}

BlobEntry { key, blob, mime, width?, height?, updatedAt }
```

> **Width/height go top-level**, not into `style`. RF v12's `NodeResizer` writes them on `node.width` / `node.height`. Persisting top-level prevents a resized card collapsing back to content-intrinsic size on reload/undo.

## `SceneStore` API

`sceneStore` singleton wraps the Dexie tables.

- `await sceneStore.init()` — counts snapshots, sets `cursor` to highest id (latest). Called once from `usePipelineEngine`.
- `pushSnapshot(snap)` — if `cursor > 0` delete every snapshot `> cursor` (forward history wiped on new edit, classic VCS) → insert with `Date.now()` → cursor = new id → trim to `MAX_SNAPSHOTS = 80`.
- `undo()` / `redo()` — find latest snapshot `<` / lowest `>` cursor, move cursor, return.
- `currentSnapshot()` — fetch by current cursor, or last snapshot if cursor unset.
- Blobs: `putBlob(key, blob, meta?)`, `putDataUrl(key, dataUrl, meta?)`, `getBlob(key)`, `getDataUrl(key)` (FileReader → base64).
- `clearAll()` — drop both tables, reset cursor.

## History flow (`useSceneHistory`)

`useSceneHistory({ pages, activePageId, replaceScene, engineRef, pinnedIds, setPinnedIds, getViewport, setViewport })` returns:
- `serializeScene()` → `ScenePayload`. Active page captures fresh viewport via `getViewport()`; inactive keep stored viewport. Stamps `manifestVersion: PUBLISH_MANIFEST_VERSION` so consumers can fail-closed on future bumps.
- `persistBlobs()` — writes image/segmentation blobs to the `blobs` table. Walks every page; clones skipped.
- `pushSnapshot(label?)` — debounced (`SNAPSHOT_DEBOUNCE_MS = 1200`). Skips when `isRestoringRef.current === true`.
- `applySnapshot(snap, engine)` — restore. Migrates legacy flat snapshots into a single `Main` page → `replaceScene(pages, activePageId)`.
- `handleUndo()` / `handleRedo()`.

### Auto-save trigger

`NodeEditor.useEffect([pages, activePageId, pin.pinnedIds, engineReady])` calls `pushSnapshot()`. Pan/zoom doesn't observe `pages` (RF drives viewport through its own store), so `onMoveEnd` from RF also calls `pushSnapshot()`. Both paths share the same debounce timer.

### Serialisation

For each page, walk every node, copy `id / type / position / data` (deep-copy `params`). Skip the `imageUrl / segPoints / etc.` processor-state copy for clones. Pull explicit `width / height` from RF node fields. For `image` nodes, look up running `ImageProcessor` and write `imageUrl: 'img:<nodeId>'` if a URL is loaded (blob payload via `persistBlobs()`). For `segmentation` nodes, look up `SegmentationProcessor` and write `segPoints / segPolygon / segMaskKey` if a mask exists. Cast edges directly to `SerializedEdge`. Active page: `getViewport()`; inactive: keep `page.viewport`.

### Restore (`applySnapshot`)

```
isRestoringRef.current = true
for page of currentPages, n of page.nodes: if (!n.data.cloneOf) engine.removeNode(n.id)

incomingPages = snap.pages ?? [{ id:'p_1', name:'Main', nodes:snap.nodes, edges:snap.edges, viewport:snap.viewport }]
setNodeIdCounter(max(snap.nodeIdCounter, maxNodeIdAcrossPages(incomingPages)))
setPageIdCounterFromPages(incomingPages)

for page of incomingPages, sn of page.nodes:
    isClone = !!sn.data.cloneOf
    if (!isClone && !PROCESSOR_CATALOG[sn.data.processor]) continue   // unknown processor → skip
    if (!isClone):
        engine.addNode(sn.id, sn.data.processor, { ...sn.data.params })
        if image: load blob → setImageUrl
        if segmentation: restore points/polygon/mask
    push to restoredPage.nodes
filter page.edges to only endpoints that survived ON THIS PAGE → restoredPage.edges (stamps type='editableStep')

replaceScene(restoredPages, snap.activePageId ?? restoredPages[0].id)
restore pinnedIds, set viewport from active page (rAF-deferred to wait for ReactFlow remount)
isRestoringRef.current = false
```

In-place migrations (mutates `sn.data.params` before engine sees them):
- **`eventEmitter` / `tapZone` event ids.** Pre-publish-plane snapshots didn't carry `id` / `label`. Empty/missing → deterministic defaults keyed off the node id (`evt_<n>` / `tap_<n>` from `n_<int>`) so external glue / restored snapshots stay stable and the publish duplicate-id check stays satisfied.

Three invariants:
- **Skip unknown processor types.** `addNode` warns; node dropped. Edges to dropped nodes filtered by per-page `aliveIds` check; `resolveSceneForEngine` later drops clone-source edges.
- **Subscribers stay attached.** `removeNode + addNode` of the same id never tears down React subscribers (`nodeListeners` keyed by id — see `node-engine.mdc`).
- **Clones never reach `engine.addNode`.** Restoring with clones produces RF nodes only; engine sees clone-rewritten edges through the next `engine.setEdges` from the engine-sync effect.

## ID counter healing

Node IDs `n_<int>`, page IDs `p_<int>`. Module-level counters in `node-editor/constants.ts` (nodes) and `node-editor/sceneResolver.ts` (pages):

```ts
nextId(); getNodeIdCounter(); setNodeIdCounter(v); maxNodeIdNumber(nodes)
nextPageId(); setPageIdCounterFromPages(pages); maxNodeIdAcrossPages(pages)
```

Both counters MUST never fall behind the live max suffix — otherwise `nextId()` hands out an existing id and `setNodes([...nds, dup])` silently drops the original (RF dedupes by `id`). Historical bug: "looks like a node-count limit, every add deletes one of the first nodes."

Guards:
- `applySnapshot` syncs node counter to `Math.max(snap.nodeIdCounter, maxNodeIdAcrossPages(incomingPages))` and page counter via `setPageIdCounterFromPages(incomingPages)` — heals even snapshots with counter at 0.
- `NodeEditor.onAddFromPopover` runs `setNodeIdCounter(Math.max(getNodeIdCounter(), maxNodeIdNumber(allNodes_acrossPages)))` just before minting — heals an open session without reload, and uses **all pages** so a node minted on page B can't collide with one from page A.
- `exportScene` writes the live `getNodeIdCounter()`, not 0.

## Export / Import

`NodeEditor.exportScene()` → `SceneFile { pages, activePageId, nodeIdCounter, pinnedIds }` downloaded as `scene.json`. Each `image` node's URL preserved from the live processor (`proc.loadedUrl`), not the blob key — JSON portable across tabs/users only when URL is public (data URLs inlined fully).

`importScene()` accepts both shapes:
- new: `pages[]`, `activePageId`;
- legacy: flat `nodes / edges / viewport` — wrapped into a single `Main` page (same migration path as Dexie restore).

After load: `applySnapshot` → `persistBlobs` → `pushSnapshot('import')` so the imported scene becomes a real history entry.

`clearScene()` removes every real engine node, resets to a single empty `Main` page, clears both Dexie tables.

## Not persisted

- Engine internals (output cache, dirty set, RT pool, geometry cache).
- Ephemeral processor state (`EnvelopeProcessor.clips`, `LogProcessor.lastSmoothed`).
- Pixi assets cache — image URLs reload via `Assets.load` on restore.

## Pitfalls

- New `data` field without `serializeScene` update → lost on next snapshot. Most fields go through `data: { ...n.data }` auto, but processor-sourced fields (image URL, segmentation mask) need explicit copy.
- New SLOT or processor → update `project-overview.mdc` and `product-vision.mdc`. Old snapshots with removed types log warning and skip (acceptable breaking change, document). Auto-migration would live in `applySnapshot` (`pages` migration is the canonical example).
- `engine.addNode` for a clone → phantom processor that never executes. Always check `if (!n.data.cloneOf)` in snapshot/restore/copy-paste paths.
- Treating `nodeIdCounter: 0` as missing → it's a real value from older exports. `applySnapshot`'s healing handles it.
- `putBlob('foo:<id>', ...)` without `data.fooKey = 'foo:<id>'` → `applySnapshot` won't load it.
- Bypassing the debounce by calling `pushSnapshot` directly → hits `MAX_SNAPSHOTS = 80` cap; older history trimmed faster than expected.
- New top-level snapshot field without `serializeScene` AND `applySnapshot` → silently dropped on undo/redo. `pages` / `activePageId` is the canonical pattern.
- Bumping `SceneDB.version` without a migration callback → existing users fail to open the DB. Add `db.version(2).stores({ ... }).upgrade(tx => ...)`.
